[{:db/id -1 :doc/id "business-openrouter-provider-billing-terms-20260908" :doc/title "Owner-confirmed billing contact payment and Modal contract basis" :doc/as-of "2026-09-08" :source/dataset "business" :doc/body "## Billing and Modal contract basis confirmed by owner — 2026-09-08\nBilling contact email: j@awai.network (the chat's escaped at-sign is normalized).\nSelected payment method: credit card. This records the owner's selection; it does not establish OpenRouter's accepted settlement arrangement, a configured automatic top-up, a card on file, or a successful transaction. Do not infer any authorization to transfer funds or collect payment from this declaration.\nModal contract basis: the ordinary published standard agreement, with no bespoke Service Order, negotiated exception or resale permission assumed. This resolves the earlier request to identify the intended contract basis; do not keep a negotiated Service Order as an unconditional onboarding prerequisite. The standard terms and actual Murakumo-managed backup architecture still need to be assessed together. Contract selection alone is not evidence that a particular resale/direct-access arrangement is permitted. Do not expose Modal credentials or direct service access to OpenRouter callers. Source for the agreement previously reviewed: https://modal.com/legal/terms .\nThe requested billing email, payment-method selection and Modal contract-basis information are now supplied. Remaining work is operational payment integration/reconciliation and verifying the backup architecture against that standard agreement, alongside the existing technical readiness gates. No card was added or charged, no contract was signed, and no application was submitted by this update.\n"}]
